From e2776b9199e7687966ee84981db619f194b76fea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:33:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): bound artifact custody I/O, upload only declared
 artifacts, keep copies on the task's board [daveey]

Follow-ups from the independent review of #2910 (card t_01a1d88201a36e8e).

1. No large-file I/O under the board write lock. record_files ran inside
   complete_task's / request_review's write_txn and SHA256-hashed (and for
   large scratch files copied + fsynced) every declared artifact and absolute
   evidence ref with no size bound, so a multi-GB checkpoint held the
   board-wide SQLite write lock and could fail other writers past the 120 s
   busy timeout. New kanban_artifact_prestage reads files over
   KANBAN_ATTACHMENT_MAX_BYTES before write_txn (digest, and for managed
   scratch a durable copy under a hidden temp name). Under the lock
   record_files re-verifies stat identity (dev, inode, size, mtime_ns) and only
   renames the copy. A large file that changed or failed its pre-lock read is
   never read under the lock: scratch fails closed (ArtifactPreservationError,
   task stays running), elsewhere the record carries size + a "not hashed"
   warning. Unclaimed temp copies are removed on exit.
2. The gateway notifier digests receipt files via asyncio.to_thread, off the
   event loop.
3. Records carry role=artifact|evidence. Only declared artifacts become native
   chat uploads (pre-#2910 behaviour); evidence keeps custody (attachment,
   digest) without an upload. Evidence refs that name no file (API routes,
   /path:123, "/repo commit ...", /healthz, existing directories) get no
   receipt record and so no "File missing" notice line; missing exact paths,
   scratch refs and declared artifacts still warn.
4. Attachment and retained copies resolve the task's board (scratch workspace
   board, else the connection's board) instead of the current board.

RED (8 failing before the fix): tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_artifact_custody_bounds.py
- large file read while write lock held (scratch + external)
- changed-after-pre-lock-read file claimed with a digest / no fail-closed
- evidence refs uploaded to chat and /api route recorded
- copies under the default board's attachments for a card on board "other"
- delivery_paths ran on the event-loop thread
GREEN: the same 9 tests pass; 75 related test files (1525 tests) pass. Two
existing tests updated for the moved internals (pre-lock copy failure now
injected at prestage._read; notifier tests keep sqlite fixtures on their
own thread).
